---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import DocsSidebar from "../../components/DocsSidebar.astro";
import BadgeDemo from "../../components/demos/BadgeDemo";
import BadgePlayground from "../../components/demos/BadgePlayground";

---

<BaseLayout title="Badge" withSidebar>
  <DocsSidebar slot="sidebar" />
  <div class="docs-prose">
    <h1>Badge</h1>
    <p>
      A small status chip. There's no HTML element for "badge",
      <code>&lt;span&gt;</code> is the honest choice for an inline,
      semantically neutral run of text that only needs presentational
      styling, one of the rare cases here without a more specific native
      anchor.
    </p>

    <div class="docs-example">
      <BadgeDemo client:visible />
    </div>

    <h2>Icons</h2>
    <p>
      Put an icon straight inside, before or after the text, or on its own.
      Any <code>&lt;svg&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;img&gt;</code> or icon
      component from your own set works; Kernel doesn't ship one. Whichever
      end holds an icon turns it into a <code>1lh</code> slot, pulled in
      until it sits the same distance from the side as from the top and
      bottom, so it's concentric with the rounded end. The icon is drawn
      at <code>--kernel-icon-size</code> inside that slot, and
      <code>--kernel-icon-stroke-width</code> can even out an outline
      set's stroke, so one pair of tokens makes any icon set look at home.
    </p>
    <p>
      The rest is optical too. Padding grows by the width the rounded ends
      cut away. The radius follows <code>--kernel-radius-control</code>
      but never goes past a true half-height pill. Capitals are centred
      using the font's cap height, so a font with lopsided ascent and
      descent metrics doesn't sit low.
    </p>

    <h2>Playground</h2>
    <p>Toggle every adjustable prop and watch the component — and the code — update live.</p>
    <BadgePlayground client:visible />

    
    <h2>Props</h2>
    <div class="docs-table-scroll"><table class="docs-table">
      <caption>Props for Badge.</caption>
      <thead><tr><th scope="col">Prop</th><th scope="col">Type</th><th scope="col">Default</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td><code>variant</code></td><td>"neutral" | "accent" | "success" | "warning" | "danger"</td><td>"neutral"</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table></div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
